summary.value:
This paper considers the optimization of the LogSumExp objective function. The idea is to replace the KL-divergence by a safe KL-entropy term in the Gibbs variational principle of the LogSumExp function. The paper derives the approximation and smoothness properties of the rescaled SoftPlus formulation, while preserving convexity. The approximation to LogSumExp can be solved via stochastic gradient methods. Applications to entropic optimal transport (EOT) and distributionally robust optimization (DRO) are demonstrated.

The reviewers raised several common weakness and questions:

- novelty of the rescaled SoftPlus approximation;
- lack of comparison with prior techniques for optimizing or bounding LogSumExp;
- empirical baselines are weak.
